Phase 12 – Export Center (Excel Report Generator)

Settings Page Enhancement – Multi-Sheet Excel Export

Objective

Introduce a centralized Export Center within the Settings page that allows users to generate a comprehensive Excel report for a selected Team and Fix Version.

The generated workbook should consolidate all release analysis information currently available throughout the application into a single downloadable Excel file with multiple worksheets.

The purpose is to provide Release Managers, Technical Leads, and Leadership with an offline report that can be shared, reviewed, archived, or attached to release documentation.

⸻

Business Value

Currently, information is distributed across multiple application pages:

* Review Commits
* Story Status
* Branch Cut Validation
* Deployment Readiness
* Commit Analysis
* Future SAST Reports

Users must navigate between screens to gather release information.

This enhancement provides:

* One-click export
* Offline review
* Leadership-ready reports
* Easy sharing
* Historical snapshots
* Release audit documentation

⸻

UI Enhancement – Settings Page

Create a new section in the Settings page named:

Export Center

or

Release Report Export

(Choose the most appropriate title consistent with the application’s design language.)

The section should follow the existing AT&T-themed UI and remain clean and intuitive.

⸻

Filters

Provide mandatory filters:

* Team
* Fix Version

The export should always be generated based on these two selections.

Project Key must not be used anywhere.

Only Team Key and Fix Version shall drive report generation.

⸻

