Download Action

Provide a single button:

Download Excel Report

or

Generate Excel Report

Upon clicking:

* Validate Team selection
* Validate Fix Version selection
* Read requested datasets from the database
* Generate a single Excel workbook
* Download the workbook

No additional navigation should be required.

⸻

Excel Workbook Structure

The workbook should contain one worksheet for each selected report.

⸻

Sheet 1 – Review Commits

Contains the complete Review Commit data currently displayed in the UI.

Include all review commit columns that are useful for release analysis.

⸻

Sheet 2 – Review Commit Violations

This sheet contains only failed or actionable review commit records.

Examples include:

* Missing Release Commit
* Cherry Pick Required
* Branch Cut Missing
* Compliance Violations
* Other failed validations

Successful commits should not appear on this sheet.

This sheet is intended for Release Managers to focus only on pending work.

⸻

Sheet 3 – Story Status

Contains the Release Readiness Story Status information.

Include:

* Story
* Status
* Assignee
* Reporter
* Team
* Component Count
* Other useful metadata

⸻

Sheet 4 – Branch Cut Validation

Contains Branch Cut Validation details.

Suggested columns:

* Component
* Previous Branch
* Current Branch
* Resolution Source
* Branch Cut Status
* Teams
* Stories
* User Excluded
* Validation Result

⸻

Sheet 5 – Test-3 Deployment

Deployment Readiness data for Test-3.

Include all deployment validation details currently available.

⸻

Sheet 6 – Test-4 Deployment

Deployment Readiness data for Test-4.

⸻

Sheet 7 – Stage West Deployment

Deployment Readiness data for Stage West.

⸻

Sheet 8 – Production East Deployment

Deployment Readiness data for Production East.

⸻

Sheet 9 – Production West Deployment

Deployment Readiness data for Production West.

⸻

Sheet 10 – Commit Analysis Summary

Contains component-level commit analysis metadata.

Suggested columns include:

* Component
* Stories
* Teams
* Total Commits
* Violations
* Cherry Picks
* Reverted Commits
* Missing Commits
* Compliance Status
* Analysis Result
* Remarks

Use the existing Commit Analysis metadata table as the primary data source.

⸻

Sheet 11 – SAST Report (Future)

If implemented:

Include:

* Component
* Security Score
* Critical
* High
* Medium
* Low
* Status

If not implemented:

Display a simple message indicating that SAST integration is not yet available.

⸻

Data Source

The export must use existing database tables.

The export should not call external systems such as:

* GitHub
* Kubernetes
* iTrack

The purpose of the export is to package already-generated analysis data.

⸻

Performance Requirements

The export should:

* Read only the selected datasets
* Avoid unnecessary queries
* Generate worksheets only for selected checkboxes
* Skip unselected reports entirely

This minimizes processing time for large releases.

⸻

UI/UX Recommendations

Design the Export Center using a clean card layout.

Suggested flow:

1. Select Team
2. Select Fix Version
3. Choose report sections using checkboxes
4. Click Download Excel Report

Enhancements:

* “Select All” checkbox
* “Clear All” button
* Group checkboxes by category
* Show total selected reports
* Disable unavailable reports
* Display a loading indicator while generating the workbook

⸻

Excel Formatting

The generated workbook should be presentation-ready.

Recommendations:

* Bold headers
* Frozen header row
* Auto-sized columns
* Filter enabled on all sheets
* Consistent date formatting
* Wrapped text where necessary
* Preserve logical column ordering

The workbook should require minimal manual formatting after download.

⸻

Acceptance Criteria

* Add a new Export Center section in the Settings page.
* Export is driven only by Team Key and Fix Version.
* Remove all Project Key dependency from the export flow.
* Provide checkbox-based report selection.
* Support downloading a single workbook with multiple worksheets.
* Generate worksheets only for selected reports.
* Review Commit report exports all review commit records.
* Review Commit Violations exports only actionable/failed records.
* Story Status exports release readiness story information.
* Branch Cut Validation exports complete branch validation details.
* Deployment Readiness exports separate worksheets for Test-3, Test-4, Stage West, Production East, and Production West.
* Commit Analysis Summary exports metadata from the Commit Analysis table.
* SAST worksheet supports future integration without requiring redesign.
* Export uses database records only and does not call GitHub, Kubernetes, or iTrack.
* Workbook formatting is clean, readable, and suitable for leadership presentations.
* Display progress while the workbook is being generated.
* Preserve existing application functionality without regression.

⸻

Definition of Done

* Export Center is available in the Settings page.
* Team and Fix Version are mandatory inputs.
* Report selection is checkbox-based.
* “Select All” and “Clear All” options are available.
* Workbook generation is successful for any valid selection.
* Each selected report generates a separate worksheet.
* Review Commit Violations contains only failed/actionable records.
* Deployment worksheets correctly reflect the selected environment data.
* Commit Analysis worksheet is populated from the Commit Analysis metadata table.
* SAST worksheet supports future expansion.
* Workbook formatting follows a professional reporting standard.
* No external API calls are made during export.
* Export performance remains acceptable for large releases.
* Existing application functionality remains unaffected.
